after:
Await pauses this async function until the promise supplies its result.
```typescript
async function makeGreeting(name: string): Promise<string> {
  return "Hello, " + name;
}
async function showGreeting(): Promise<void> {
  const text = await makeGreeting("Nora");
  console.log(text);
}
const demonstration = showGreeting();
```
The output is Hello, Nora. Promise<void> means showGreeting has no useful result value.
